# `xrandr --output HEADLESS-1 --off`, measured 2026-09-10 (cap1.log connection
# 6, requests 18-20): the grab, a SetCrtcConfig with mode None and an EMPTY
# output list, and SetScreenSize(16, 16, 4, 4) -- the smallest framebuffer the
# server's GetScreenSizeRange allows, because nothing is left on the screen.
#
# There is no UngrabServer on this line and that is the measurement, not an
# omission: Xwayland answered the SetScreenSize BadMatch (minor 7) and xrandr
# died inside Xlib's default error handler with the server still grabbed
# [recon/tools.md 7]. It is why a client that disconnects with a batch open has
# that batch DROPPED (design section 7.5): what it collected here is a disable
# with no enable, and applying half of it turns a screen off with nothing left
# to turn it back on.
#
# The disable's bytes are byte-identical to the disable half of --mode
# (xrandr-mode-write.hex line 2, allowing for the different ids): --off sets the
# output's mode to None and crtc_apply returns early on !crtc->mode_info.
24000100
8b1507002000000000000000d0df6331000000000000000001000000
8b07050034020000100010000400000004000000
